# Git

- Clone once. After that, `git pull --rebase origin main` at the start of a session and again before every push.
- Work on branch `g1` / `g2` / `g3` / `g4`. Only the integrator merges into `main`.
- Never force-push. Never change git config. Never commit `.env`, keys, `node_modules`, or `dist`.
- If rebase stops, fix only files you own. Leave other groups' files as they pushed them.

```
# BAD — push straight to main, or force
git push origin main
git push --force

# GOOD
git checkout g1
git pull --rebase origin main
git push -u origin g1
```
